timestamp=2026-11-04T19:19:10.240Z level=INFO run=2db649e5 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport csv\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/hospital_compensation_registry.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    rows = list(reader)\n\n# So we have:\n# 1. PAT_033 receives bereavement compensation (102700). PAT_174 has no claims but lists PAT_033 as EC. → PAT_174 is likely deceased.\n# 2. PAT_265 receives family support adjustment (101400). PAT_265 lists PAT_065 as EC. PAT_065 has no claims but exists as a patient and is listed as EC by PAT_265. Also PAT_065 lists PAT_080 as EC. → PAT_065 is likely deceased.\n\n# Are there other bereavement/family support claims?\n# Look through all compensation reasons again.\nclaims = []\nfor r in rows:\n    if r['compensation_reason']:\n        claims.append((r['patient_id'], r['compensation_reason'], r['direct_payment_usd'], r['emergency_contact_patient_id']))\nclaims.sort(key=lambda x: x[1])\nfor c in claims[:15]:\n    print(c)\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
