timestamp=2026-11-04T19:20:42.709Z level=INFO run=2db649e5 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport csv\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/hospital_compensation_registry.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    rows = list(reader)\n\n# Only PAT_065 is directly connected to a death-related claim via listers. The other confirmed deceased is PAT_174. How is PAT_174 connected to death claim? \n# PAT_174 lists PAT_033 as EC. PAT_033 receives bereavement. So the link is: deceased (PAT_174) → lists survivor as EC; survivor (PAT_033) receives bereavement. That’s the reverse direction of the other case.\n# So maybe other deceased are people who list the bereavement/family-support recipient as their EC, AND have no claims themselves. Let us look for that pattern.\n\nbereave_recipients = []\nfam_recipients = []\nfor r in rows:\n    cr = (r['compensation_reason'] or '').lower()\n    if 'bereave' in cr:\n        bereave_recipients.append(r['patient_id'])\n    if 'family support' in cr:\n        fam_recipients.append(r['patient_id'])\n\nprint('bereave:', bereave_recipients, 'family:', fam_recipients)\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
