timestamp=2026-11-04T19:21:50.293Z level=INFO run=2db649e5 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport csv\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/hospital_compensation_registry.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    rows = list(reader)\n\n# So the picture is:\n# - PAT_174 (no claims) lists PAT_033 as EC. PAT_174 is also listed as EC by PAT_032. PAT_033 receives bereavement compensation. → PAT_174 is deceased.\n# - PAT_065 (no claims) lists PAT_080 as EC. PAT_065 is also listed as EC by PAT_265, PAT_178, PAT_146. PAT_265 receives family support adjustment. → PAT_065 is deceased (likely the subject of the family support paid to PAT_265).\n# - PAT_023 (no claims) lists PAT_265 as EC. PAT_023 is also listed as EC by PAT_040. PAT_265 receives family support adjustment. → PAT_023 is also likely deceased (another subject related to the same family support payout? Or a different case where PAT_265 is the contact/recipient). Also PAT_265 is the recipient of family support and is also listed as EC by PAT_023? That means if PAT_023 is deceased, PAT_265 might be their next of kin receiving support - that fits. Also PAT_265 is the one getting the payout, so multiple people might be covered by that support? Or maybe there are multiple deceased? Or perhaps the family support is related to one deceased individual. But the data shows only one family support adjustment record under PAT_265. That’s a bit ambiguous.\n\n# Another interpretation: look at all people who have no claims and list a bereavement/family-support recipient as their EC. We found PAT_174 and PAT_023. That gives us 2. Plus the other case where the deceased is the one who IS listed as EC by the recipient? Like PAT_065 is listed as EC by PAT_265 (recipient of family support). So in that structure, deceased is the \"target EC\" of the recipient. In the other structure, deceased is the \"source\" who lists the recipient as EC.\n# Both are plausible. That gives us 3 total candidates: PAT_174, PAT_065, and also PAT_023? Also is there anyone else in the first structure (deceased lists recipient as EC)?\n# Look for other no-claim patients listing any bereavement/family support recipient as EC: we got PAT_174 (lists PAT_033, bereavement recipient) and PAT_023 (lists PAT_265, family support recipient). That’s it. Also are there other recipients? Only those two.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
