timestamp=2026-11-04T19:22:10.159Z level=INFO run=2db649e5 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport csv\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/hospital_compensation_registry.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    rows = list(reader)\n\n# So PAT_265 (family support recipient) lists PAT_065 as EC, and PAT_065 has no claims → PAT_065 is likely the deceased.\n# That’s consistent with what we thought.\n# And for PAT_033 (bereavement recipient), they list PAT_011 as EC who has claims. So the deceased is not the EC they list; instead, the deceased is someone who lists PAT_033 as EC (PAT_174) → also consistent.\n# So both patterns exist. We get two names from these: PAT_065 and PAT_174.\n# And also we have PAT_023: no claims, lists PAT_265 (family support recipient) as EC. That means if PAT_023 died, PAT_265 is their contact/beneficiary receiving family support related to PAT_023? That’s another deceased person.\n# That’s plausible. Also family support might cover dependents or multiple related deceased? Or maybe multiple family members died. Or it could be that the family support is for one death but multiple people are connected. Hard to say for sure. But this is a common type of puzzle - looking for people with no claims who are heavily referenced as ECs, and also those linked to bereavement/family support.\n# Also compare EC counts: PAT_065 has 3 listers total; PAT_174 has 1 lister (PAT_032); PAT_023 has 1 lister (PAT_040). That’s different. Also look at other no-claim patients with multiple listers - maybe they’re also deceased?\n# For example, PAT_203 has 3 listers, no claims, no connection to death payouts. Also PAT_267, PAT_273, PAT_084, PAT_126, PAT_218, PAT_262 all have 3 listers and no claims. That’s a lot of people. Why would so many have no claims but be ECs? Could be elderly or just healthy contacts - but also could be deceased. \n# Also the question just says \"Return a set of three patient IDs that are most likely to be deceased.\" Maybe the answer is PAT_065, PAT_174, and one of those high-EC-count no-claim patients? Which one?\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
